# kcmd OKF demo: throwaway push staging tree.
#
# `**/`, NOT a per-workspace list. This used to name `okf-kb-workspace/.staging/`
# only, while Track A stages into `bq-okf-workspace/.staging/` (push-track-a.ts
# uses `cwd() + '/.staging'`). Nothing was tracked purely because the tree is
# deleted on exit — one run with `OKF_KEEP_STAGING=1` followed by `git add -A`
# would have committed a full stash tree, which is rule 1 ("no stash in the
# SOURCE; the stash is a build artifact") violated by accident rather than by
# decision. Any future workspace is covered without a second edit.
**/.staging/

# Track B workspace catalog is a throwaway copy of okf-bundle, recreated by
# every push (see HANDOFF 2.7). Tracking it means the source of truth exists
# twice in git and can silently diverge — which it did.
okf-kb-workspace/catalog/

# Phase 8 Arm K workspace bundle copy (regenerated from okf-bundle)
okf-agent/armk-workspace/bundle/
